Z||000008||terryk||07-06-2000||04:25 PM||||Something just dawned on me. You have a manual trans, right?<P>I'll bet the ECM is going through the Excess Torque Management for a shift. When you downshift and press the throttle, the ECM program thinks it needs to do an automatic downshift. It looks at the MPH and TPS and decided how many gears it can drop. Then it backs off the spark, does the shift and starts raising the spark again. This is done to keep from killing the 4T60E/65E (especially on a 3-&gt;2 downshift) and to smooth out the shifts. The ECM still thinks it's controlling an automatic transmission.<P>Try this, let off throttle, do the shift, count to 3 and stab it. Does it buck when you delay the WOT?<P>$10's that's what is happening.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 07-06-2000).]||||reg||1
