Z||000022||terryk||07-08-2000||06:50 PM||||Some people are known to run the later DOHC engines on the 16149396 ECM so the manual can be used correctly and calibrations can be changed &lt;g&gt;. You loose the sequential fuel injection, drop the cam and front crank sensor, and loose the fast start (and the SFI engines are only sequential at low RPM's anyway).<P>I'm using a 95 engine with the 93 ECM. Either way, I won't need to fool anything.<P>Your engine has the larger intake to try and stop the 3000 RPM howl.<P>Terry||||reg||1
